%chk=probe_h2o_rks.chk
%mem=2GB
%nprocshared=1
#P B3LYP/6-31G NoSymm Int=NoBasisTransform SCF=(Conver=10)
# Output=MatrixElement Tran=Full Window=(2,13)

probe_h2o_rks: H2O RKS/B3LYP/6-31G, 1 frozen core, active MOs 2-13. Geometry and
basis match the h2o_rks fixture, so E(SCF) is comparable. THE POINT OF THIS JOB:
find out whether Gaussian writes a Fock-like matrix for a DFT reference. If it
does, that matrix is the Kohn-Sham matrix, contains exchange-correlation, and is
NOT the HF Fock operator -- g16dump must refuse to read it into fock_ao_*.

